      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "People have been telling me how automatic Udon blacklists aren't allowed for months, but I could not find it mentioned anywhere in VRChat's Terms of Service or Community Guidelines. It wasn't until last month when a VRChat staff member literally mentioned it on the VRChat discord server that I knew what to google for and easily found it, **Udon Moderation Tool Guidelines**. And I was surprised that the guidelines document was only listed in the World Creator Udon documentation section. No non-world creator would ever think to look there.\n\nI don't agree with how this Canny post is written. But I agree that VRChat's Terms of Service or Community Guidelines should probably have a link to related documents such as the **Udon Moderation Tool Guidelines**. This would allow non-world creators to find it easier and make better decisions when trying to find out if a world is breaking the rules or not. We can't report a world for breaking the rules, if we don't know what rules world creators have to follow.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
