      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{610d538d5303a82960a415b4|full_name}: This post is about how this issue extends far beyond just the moderation tool guidelines themselves. Every point you put forward also helps point out how problematic VRChat's stance on this is.\n\nDespite having actually been hidden, even if it wasn't inaccessible: Regardless if it's a player or a creator, if the rules are hidden away and every instance that directs us to the rules points us to somewhere else (specifically community guidelines), then how are we supposed to know what rules are being broken? Why are they hidden away, and what else is hidden that we don't know? How are these supposed to be fairly enforced if they're separated from the actual rules?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
