      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6075605abff0176ab3cf79ee|full_name}: Yes, I know. I specifically said \"related documents **such as** the Udon Moderation Tool Guidelines.\"\n\nBut you also have to remember. VRChat can change their rules whenever they want or need. You should be happy that they gave you 5 days to comply with it and information about what you had to do to be complying.\n\nWhat you should have done in this case, was to comply and then fight their ruling. Actively refusing to comply and then complaining about the consequences is foolish.\n\nAs for your blacklist issue specifically. You seem to be assuming that players on that blacklist even want to be in your world. If those blacklisted players do indeed start causing actual issues, you should report them with the needed evidence of what they did in those instances. But an even better option would probably be to just use *group public* instances, since that literally allows you to block problem players from ever joining the instance in the first place.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
