  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-07-20T15:05:39.357Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "VRChat has some secret guidelines that are literally hidden from their own playerbase, and shown to you only once you break them. How are people supposed to know what your own rules are, if you don't even display them and leave it for us to figure out what VRChat doesn't like? How many of these exist?\n\nHaving any kind of secret list of rules that you choose to enforce against players is the most self-destructive policy in any game. Shutting down games that actively make an income that violate no rules or the terms of service but on a secret rule also opens up VRChat to legal issues.\n\nIf they are \"not final\", simply display them and mention that they are subject to change, don't hide them from your players.\n\nEdit: I've written an email to VRChat about this exact concern, and literally one day later updated one of these pages accordingly without response. It's now visible in one of their documentations, along with removing whitelists (as one of my concerns) but still contain the header as it was rushed and added a 'Last Updated' part to the page. I saved a screenshot when I first received a notice, and the comparison is visible below, and deceitful actions like these continue to make players lose trust and make this post ever more concerning.\n\nhttps://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/udon/udon-moderation-tool-guidelines/\n\nGuidelines like these are also very inconsistent and even more damaging when you enforce them, when one of the top requests for 4 years is for moderation features, which VRChat has also marked interest in finally adding.\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/moderation-tools-for-world-creators\n\nPlease be transparent with your community, and please communicate with us.",
